  "interpretation": [
    "All745 publisher references contain only Latin letters after apostrophe folding. The same source texts were verified directly against both original Arrow shards.",
    "The unchanged primary WER measures normalized written agreement. It mixes word recognition, spelling, number conventions and script choice; it is not an isolated acoustic-error rate.",
    "No transliteration was performed, so neither the score after hypothetical script normalization nor the number of semantically equivalent cross-script answers is known.",
    "Shorter outputs and deletions can coexist with script mismatch; the partition does not attribute all errors in those outputs to their writing system."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The745-row published Telegram corpus retains duplicate audio under the frozen primary protocol; it is not a population-wide estimate of Uzbek accuracy.",
    "No manual listening, semantic-equivalence annotation, transliteration, alternate reference scoring or new inference was performed.",
    "Unicode script mismatch can penalize written equivalence, but its presence does not establish that other word errors in the same answer have that cause.",
    "The output-dependent partitions account for all observed errors and are descriptive only, not alternative benchmark subsets.",
    "Results describe the frozen deployable configurations and do not isolate architecture, precision, frontend or language-conditioning effects."
  ],
